        {
          "insert": "Knowledge intake — the librarian"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-40-15-intro": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-40-15-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "One pipeline, one librarian. Every inbound item — a past PR, a discord pull, a worker completion — passes through a single librarian agent (the knowledge-curator grown up; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/knowledge/curator/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "): it reads the item, figures out what was learned, infers the mapping (subject + scope), links the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/55-knowledge-graph-redesign/40-knowledge-stores/20-smashwiki-corpus"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and catalogs the learning where it belongs in the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ledger",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/55-knowledge-graph-redesign/40-knowledge-stores/10-knowledge-ledger"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The worker writes no report of its own: on completion the librarian takes the transcript and run state — every attempt, score, and diff — and condenses it, filing each attempt into the attempt ledger and cataloging any learnings into the knowledge ledger. Everything passes through this one intake — into the brain of the harness."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-intake-backfill-xref": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-intake-backfill-xref",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Backfill runs this same librarian in bulk mode over each source's full history — present-anchored, timestamp-superseded. The process and its differences from live flow are detailed in the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "migration map",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/55-knowledge-graph-redesign/70-migration-map"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
