    "b-55-kgr-intake-grounding-callout": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-intake-grounding-callout",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Current-code grounding (2026-08-10)",
        "tone": "info"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Today's knowledge-curator reads none of this: its deterministic stage condenses DB rows plus the worker's short handoff note, and its LLM stage sees at most 40 already-condensed records. The librarian's defining upgrade is exactly this gap — transcript-grounded condensation, attempt filing from checkpoints, and creating the tactic → score-delta association that currently exists nowhere. One repair is prerequisite: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pi_sessions.session_file",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " paths are stale (they point at the pre-migration repo), so the transcript linkage must be fixed before the worker door can open."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-40-15-process": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-40-15-process",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "librarian reads new material from a door (run transcript + state · PR extract · discord batch)"
          },
          {
            "text": "librarian infers proposals {statement, subject (+scope), origin, evidence[], confidence} and maps them to targets"
          },
          {
            "text": "every worker attempt is filed into the attempt ledger as observed — learnings are the byproduct, attempts are always recorded"
          },
          {
            "text": "curator validates every evidence ref resolves"
          },
          {
            "text": "append to the knowledge ledger as proposed"
          },
          {
            "text": "corroboration per origin trust policy (human: 1 confirm; ai: 2 confirms or 1 strong)"
          },
          {
            "text": "staleness via content-hash at rebuild; graduation rides match PRs"
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-40-15-decision": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-40-15-decision",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-10) — intake mirrors the existing curator",
        "tone": "decision"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Knowledge intake is the same mechanism as today's knowledge-curator agent, extended: the three doors (past PR, discord pull, worker completion) all normalize into one proposal shape and one append path. No new agent species — the curator grows doors."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-40-15-decision-librarian": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-40-15-decision-librarian",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-10) — the librarian",
        "tone": "decision"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The store is maintained by one librarian-like agent. The worker writes no report: the librarian condenses the transcript and run state of everything that was done — every attempt is filed into the attempt ledger, and learnings (if any) are inferred, mapped (subject + scope), evidence-linked, and cataloged. Inference happens at intake, not at emission. When a target is picked back up, every prior attempt on it is visible."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
